{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming for Stirling numbers of the second kind.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # stirling[i][j] stores S(i, j), Stirling number of the second kind\n    stirling = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        stirling[i][0] = 0  # S(i, 0) = 0 for i > 0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling[i][j] = stirling[i - 1][j - 1] + j * stirling[i - 1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n\n    bell_n = sum(stirling[n][k] for k in range(n + 1))\n    return bell_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array is monotonic (either non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    Handles empty and single-element arrays as monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    increasing = True\n    decreasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] > arr[i-1]:\n            decreasing = False\n        elif arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            increasing = False\n\n        # If the array is neither strictly increasing nor strictly decreasing at any point, it's not monotonic.\n        if not increasing and not decreasing:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
