{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\n# Initialize a memoization dictionary for storing computed Newman-Conway sequence values.\n_memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth number of the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        # Return memoized value if already computed.\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate P(n) using the recursive formula and store the result.\n    result = sequence(sequence(n - 1)) + sequence(n - sequence(n - 1))\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Newman-Conway sequence number using memoization.\n    It returns the integer value of P(n) for a given positive integer n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    # Iterate from 3 up to n, calculating each term.\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        # Apply the Newman-Conway recurrence relation: P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1))\n        memo[i] = memo[memo[i-1]] + memo[i-memo[i-1]]\n\n    return memo[n]"}
