{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "```python\nclass IntegerArray:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates an array of integers and provides methods for calculation.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, elements: list[int]):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the IntegerArray with the given list of integers.\"\"\"\n        self.elements = elements\n\n    def findMaxProductSubarray(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of any contiguous subarray.\n        It handles various scenarios like negatives, zeros, and single elements.\"\"\"\n        if not self.elements:\n            return 0\n\n        max_so_far = self.elements[0]\n        min_so_far = self.elements[0]\n        result = self.elements[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(self.elements)):\n            current_num = self.elements[i]\n\n            # Update max_so_far and min_so_far, considering current number and products.\n            temp_max_so_far = max(current_num, max_so_far * current_num, min_so_far * current_num)\n            min_so_far = min(current_num, max_so_far * current_num, min_so_far * current_num)\n\n            max_so_far = temp_max_so_far\n\n            result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n        return result\n\ndef max_subarray_product(input_array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray from the input array.\n    This function serves as the system's entry point, utilizing the IntegerArray component.\"\"\"\n\n    integer_array_instance = IntegerArray(input_array)\n    max_product = integer_array_instance.findMaxProductSubarray()\n\n    return max_product\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_subarray_product(input_array: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    This function handles positive, negative, and zero values efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_so_far = input_array[0]\n    max_ending_here = input_array[0]\n    min_ending_here = input_array[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(input_array)):\n        num = input_array[i]\n\n        temp_max_ending_here = max_ending_here\n\n        max_ending_here = max(num, max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n        min_ending_here = min(num, temp_max_ending_here * num, min_ending_here * num)\n\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_ending_here)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
