{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "```python\ndef max_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of an increasing subsequence within the given array.\n    Uses a dynamic programming approach to find the largest product.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0  # Per the problem description, handle edge for empty array, though design implies non-empty.\n\n    dp_products = [0] * n\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp_products[i] = arr[i]  # Initialize with the element itself (subsequence of length 1).\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:  # Check if arr[i] can extend a subsequence ending at arr[j].\n                potential_product = dp_products[j] * arr[i]\n                dp_products[i] = max(dp_products[i], potential_product)\n\n    return max(dp_products)\n```\n"}
