{"task_id": "Mbpp/563", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_values(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts substrings enclosed within double quotation marks from an input string.\n    Returns a list of these extracted values, without the quotes.\n    \"\"\"\n    extracted_values = []\n    in_quote = False\n    current_chars = []\n\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char == '\"':\n            if in_quote:\n                # Found closing quote, append the accumulated characters as a string.\n                extracted_values.append(\"\".join(current_chars))\n                current_chars = []\n                in_quote = False\n            else:\n                # Found opening quote, start accumulating characters.\n                in_quote = True\n        elif in_quote:\n            # Inside quotes, so this character is part of the current value.\n            current_chars.append(char)\n\n    return extracted_values\n```"}
