{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if sub_list is a contiguous sublist of main_list.\n    Handles empty sublists and cases where sub_list is longer than main_list.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BR2: Empty sublist is considered a sublist of any list.\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n\n    # BR3: If the sublist is longer than the main list, it cannot be a sublist.\n    if len(sub_list) > len(main_list):\n        return False\n\n    len_main = len(main_list)\n    len_sub = len(sub_list)\n\n    # Iterate through main_list to find a matching contiguous slice (BR1).\n    for i in range(len_main - len_sub + 1):\n        if main_list[i : i + len_sub] == sub_list:\n            return True\n\n    # If the loop completes, no match was found.\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(main_list, sub_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if sub_list is a sublist of main_list.\n    An empty list is a sublist of any list; elements must appear consecutively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i : i + m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
