{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(t1: tuple, t2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the symmetric difference between two tuples, preserving relative order.\n    Elements unique to t1 appear first, followed by elements unique to t2.\n    \"\"\"\n    set_t1 = set(t1)\n    set_t2 = set(t2)\n\n    unique_to_t1_list = []\n    # Collect elements from t1 that are not in t2, maintaining their original order.\n    for element in t1:\n        if element not in set_t2:\n            unique_to_t1_list.append(element)\n\n    unique_to_t2_list = []\n    # Collect elements from t2 that are not in t1, maintaining their original order.\n    for element in t2:\n        if element not in set_t1:\n            unique_to_t2_list.append(element)\n\n    # Concatenate the lists and convert to a tuple for the final result.\n    return tuple(unique_to_t1_list + unique_to_t2_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements that are present in one tuple but not in the other.\n    Returns a tuple containing all dissimilar elements, with no duplicates.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n\n    only_in_tuple1 = set1 - set2\n    only_in_tuple2 = set2 - set1\n\n    dissimilar_elements = only_in_tuple1.union(only_in_tuple2)\n\n    return tuple(dissimilar_elements)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/580", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_even(tup: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Recursively extracts even integers from a nested tuple, preserving its structure.\n    Non-integer and non-tuple elements are ignored, and empty resulting sub-tuples are omitted.\"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for item in tup:\n        if isinstance(item, int):\n            if item % 2 == 0:\n                result_list.append(item)\n        elif isinstance(item, tuple):\n            sub_tuple_result = extract_even(item)\n            if sub_tuple_result:\n                result_list.append(sub_tuple_result)\n    return tuple(result_list)\n```"}
