{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef perfect_squares(start: int, end: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a sorted list of perfect squares within a specified inclusive integer range.\n    An empty list is returned if no perfect squares are found or the range is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    if start > end:\n        return []\n\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n\n    # Calculate the effective start for square root, ensuring it's non-negative.\n    effective_start_for_sqrt = max(0, start)\n\n    # Determine the smallest integer whose square is greater than or equal to 'effective_start_for_sqrt'.\n    current_num = math.ceil(math.sqrt(effective_start_for_sqrt))\n\n    # Iterate upwards, calculating squares and adding them if within the range.\n    while True:\n        square = int(current_num * current_num)\n\n        if square > end:\n            break\n\n        if square >= start:\n            perfect_squares_list.append(square)\n\n        current_num += 1\n\n    return perfect_squares_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef perfect_squares(num1: int, num2: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all perfect squares between num1 and num2 (inclusive).\n    Returns a list of perfect squares, sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = min(num1, num2)\n    upper_bound = max(num1, num2)\n\n    if upper_bound < 0:\n        return []\n\n    actual_lower_bound = max(0, lower_bound)\n\n    start_root = math.ceil(math.sqrt(actual_lower_bound))\n    end_root = math.floor(math.sqrt(upper_bound))\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(int(start_root), int(end_root) + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        if actual_lower_bound <= square <= upper_bound:\n            result.append(square)\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
