{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "```python\ndef armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is equal to the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the total number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False  # Negative numbers are not considered Armstrong numbers by definition.\n\n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n\n    sum_of_powers = 0\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return sum_of_powers == number\n```"}
