{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    # Calculates the nth Bell number using Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    # The dp table stores S(i, j), the number of ways to partition i elements into j non-empty subsets.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        dp[i][0] = 0 # S(i, 0) is 0 for i > 0\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + j * dp[i-1][j]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n.\n    nth_bell_num = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        nth_bell_num += dp[n][k]\n\n    return nth_bell_num"}
