{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming.\n    Bell numbers count the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    bell = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell[0] = 1\n\n    # Iteratively calculate Bell numbers using the recurrence B_{i+1} = sum_{k=0 to i} C(i, k) * B_k.\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bell_val = 0\n        binomial_coeff = 1  # C(i, 0) is always 1\n        for k in range(i + 1):\n            current_bell_val += binomial_coeff * bell[k]\n            # Calculate C(i, k+1) from C(i, k) efficiently.\n            if k < i:\n                binomial_coeff = binomial_coeff * (i - k) // (k + 1)\n        bell[i + 1] = current_bell_val\n\n    return bell[n]\n```\n"}
