{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset where every pair (a, b) satisfies a % b == 0 or b % a == 0.\n    This implementation uses dynamic programming after sorting unique elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    sorted_unique_numbers = sorted(list(set(numbers)))\n    n = len(sorted_unique_numbers)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with sorted_unique_numbers[i].\n    dp = [1] * n\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if sorted_unique_numbers[i] % sorted_unique_numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n\n    return max(dp)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise modulo operation on two tuples of the same length.\n    Raises ValueError for length mismatch or ZeroDivisionError for division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    results = []\n    for val1, val2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if val2 == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(\"Cannot perform modulo by zero.\")\n        results.append(val1 % val2)\n\n    return tuple(results)\n```"}
