{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list, list2: list, n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two sorted lists of size n.\n    The median is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th elements\n    from the conceptually merged and sorted list (1-based indexing).\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n\n    # Variables to store the n-th and (n+1)-th elements (1-based indexing)\n    n_th_element = None\n    n_plus_1_th_element = None\n\n    # Iterate 2*n times to find elements up to the (2*n)-th position.\n    # We are interested in elements at 0-based indices (n-1) and n.\n    for count in range(2 * n):\n        current_val = 0\n\n        # Determine which list to pick the next smallest element from\n        if i < n and j < n:\n            if list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n                current_val = list1[i]\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                current_val = list2[j]\n                j += 1\n        elif i < n:  # list2 is exhausted, pick from list1\n            current_val = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # list1 is exhausted, pick from list2\n            current_val = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n        # Save the element if it corresponds to the n-th or (n+1)-th position\n        if count == n - 1:\n            n_th_element = current_val\n        elif count == n:\n            n_plus_1_th_element = current_val\n\n    # Calculate and return the average as a float\n    return float(n_th_element + n_plus_1_th_element) / 2.0\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/631", "solution": "def replace_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Transforms a string by replacing whitespace with underscores, or underscores with spaces.\n    The modification depends on specific conditions of the input string, with whitespace replacement taking precedence.\"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    has_whitespace = False\n    processed_for_whitespace = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isspace():\n            has_whitespace = True\n            processed_for_whitespace.append('_')\n        else:\n            processed_for_whitespace.append(char)\n\n    if has_whitespace:\n        return \"\".join(processed_for_whitespace)\n\n    if '_' in input_string:\n        return input_string.replace('_', ' ')\n\n    return input_string"}
