{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def _heapify(arr: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maintains the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index `i` in `arr`\n    of size `n`. It ensures the largest element is at the root.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\ndef heap_sort(arr: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the given list `arr` in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    The sorting is performed in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Build a max-heap.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Move current root to end\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Call _heapify on the reduced heap"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list[int], size: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of bitwise XOR for all unique pairs in a list of numbers.\n    Returns 0 if the list has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if size < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(size - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, size):\n            total_xor_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n\n    return total_xor_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(list_of_numbers: list[int], list_length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of bitwise XOR operations for all unique pairs in a list.\"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n\n    for i in range(list_length):\n        num1 = list_of_numbers[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, list_length):\n            num2 = list_of_numbers[j]\n            current_xor = num1 ^ num2\n            total_xor_sum += current_xor\n\n    return total_xor_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list in-place using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It builds a max-heap and then extracts elements one by one.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    # Helper function to maintain the max-heap property\n    def _heapify(arr: list, heap_size: int, i: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Maintains the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\n        Compares the root with its children and performs swaps as needed.\n        \"\"\"\n        largest = i\n        left = 2 * i + 1\n        right = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left < heap_size and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < heap_size and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            _heapify(arr, heap_size, largest)\n\n    # Helper function to build a max-heap from an unsorted list\n    def _build_max_heap(arr: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Transforms the input list into a max-heap by heapifying all non-leaf nodes.\n        Starts from the last non-leaf node and goes up to the root.\n        \"\"\"\n        start_index = n // 2 - 1\n        for i in range(start_index, -1, -1):\n            _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # 1. Build a max-heap from the input_list\n    _build_max_heap(input_list)\n\n    # 2. Extract elements one by one from the heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\\\n        # Swap current root (largest element) with the last element\n        input_list[i], input_list[0] = input_list[0], input_list[i]\n        # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n        _heapify(input_list, i, 0)\n\n    return input_list\n```"}
