{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "```python\ndef maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average path cost in a square matrix.\n    Paths start at (0,0), end at (N-1, N-1), moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    if N == 0:\n        return 0.0\n\n    # DP table to store maximum cumulative costs to reach each cell.\n    dp = [[0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Initialize the top-left cell.\n    dp[0][0] = matrix[0][0]\n\n    # Fill the first row (only move right).\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][j] = dp[0][j-1] + matrix[0][j]\n\n    # Fill the first column (only move down).\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        dp[i][0] = dp[i-1][0] + matrix[i][0]\n\n    # Fill the rest of the DP table.\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(1, N):\n            dp[i][j] = matrix[i][j] + max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    # The maximum total cost is at the bottom-right cell.\n    max_total_cost = dp[N-1][N-1]\n\n    # All valid paths have the same number of cells (2*N - 1).\n    num_cells = (2 * N) - 1\n\n    # Calculate and return the maximum average cost.\n    return float(max_total_cost) / num_cells\n\n```"}
