{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with exactly n digits.\n    It iteratively calculates triangular numbers until one with n digits is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        # Calculate triangular number T_k using the formula k * (k + 1) / 2\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n\n        # Determine the number of digits in the triangular number\n        # by converting it to a string and getting its length.\n        num_digits = len(str(triangular_number))\n\n        # If the current triangular number has exactly n digits, return its index k.\n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n\n        # Increment k to check the next triangular number.\n        k += 1\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple into a dictionary using adjacent elements as key-value pairs.\n    If the input tuple has an odd number of elements, the last element is ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_dict = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple), 2):\n        if i + 1 < len(input_tuple):\n            key = input_tuple[i]\n            value = input_tuple[i+1]\n            result_dict[key] = value\n    return result_dict\n```"}
