{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_triangular_number(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the triangular number T_k for a given index k.\"\"\"\n    return k * (k + 1) // 2\n\ndef _get_number_of_digits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Determines the number of decimal digits in a given integer.\"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n    return len(str(number))\n\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with exactly n digits.\n    This function iteratively searches for the first triangular number that meets the digit count.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = _calculate_triangular_number(k)\n        current_digits = _get_number_of_digits(triangular_number)\n\n        if current_digits == n:\n            return k\n\n        k += 1\n\n```"}
