{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list k items to the right, returning a new rotated list.\n    Handles empty lists and `k` values greater than list length using modulo arithmetic.\"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_k = k % list_length\n\n    # Split the list into the portion that moves to the front (tail)\n    # and the portion that follows it (head).\n    tail_part = input_list[list_length - effective_k:]\n    head_part = input_list[:list_length - effective_k]\n\n    # Concatenate the parts to form the new, rotated list.\n    return tail_part + head_part\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with elements reordered according to the rotation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(input_list)\n    effective_rotation_count = rotation_count % n\n\n    split_point = n - effective_rotation_count\n\n    # Concatenate the last part of the list with the first part\n    rotated_list = input_list[split_point:] + input_list[:split_point]\n\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
