{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every digit it contains.\n    Returns a list of such integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_divisible_by_all_digits(n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if an integer n is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\n        Returns True if it is, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        s_n = str(n)\n        for char_digit in s_n:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            if digit == 0:\n                return False\n            if n % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_divisible_by_all_digits(num):\n            result.append(num)\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/753", "solution": "```python\ndef min_k(data: list[tuple[str, int]], k: int) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts k tuples with the smallest integer values from a list, sorted in ascending order.\n    Handles edge cases for k and empty input lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= 0 or not data:\n        return []\n\n    # Create a sorted copy of the data, ordered by the integer value.\n    sorted_data = sorted(data, key=lambda x: x[1])\n\n    # Determine the number of elements to return, handling k larger than list length.\n    num_to_return = min(k, len(sorted_data))\n\n    # Return the slice of the sorted data.\n    return sorted_data[:num_to_return]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number using an iterative approach.\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    j_prev2 = 0  # Represents J(i-2)\n    j_prev1 = 1  # Represents J(i-1)\n\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        current_j = j_prev1 + 2 * j_prev2\n        j_prev2 = j_prev1\n        j_prev1 = current_j\n\n    return j_prev1\n```"}
