{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string represents a decimal number with exactly two digits after the decimal point.\n    Returns True for valid formats like '123.11' or '-0.01', otherwise False.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The regex pattern matches an optional sign, one or more digits, a literal decimal point,\n    # and exactly two digits, from the start to the end of the string.\n    pattern = r\"^[+-]?\\\\d+\\\\.\\\\d{2}$\"\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(pattern, input_string))\n```"}
