{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses a given string.\n    Comparison is case-sensitive as per BR3.\n    \"\"\"\n    return s[::-1]\n\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of unique reverse string pairs in the provided list.\n    Uses a frequency map to track strings and adhere to BR2 (each string used once).\n    \"\"\"\n    freq_map = {}\n    for s in string_list:\n        freq_map[s] = freq_map.get(s, 0) + 1\n\n    reverse_pairs_count = 0\n    # Iterate over a copy of keys to safely modify dict values during iteration\n    for current_string in list(freq_map.keys()):\n        if freq_map[current_string] == 0:\n            # This string (or all its instances) has already been paired\n            continue\n\n        reversed_string = _reverse_string(current_string)\n\n        if current_string == reversed_string:\n            # This is a palindrome. Count pairs based on its frequency.\n            reverse_pairs_count += freq_map[current_string] // 2\n            freq_map[current_string] = 0 # Mark all instances as used\n        else:\n            # Not a palindrome. Look for its exact reverse.\n            if reversed_string in freq_map and freq_map[reversed_string] > 0:\n                num_pairs = min(freq_map[current_string], freq_map[reversed_string])\n                reverse_pairs_count += num_pairs\n                freq_map[current_string] -= num_pairs\n                freq_map[reversed_string] -= num_pairs\n\n    return reverse_pairs_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/758", "solution": "from collections import Counter\n\ndef unique_sublists(input_list: list[list]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique sublists within a list of lists.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list where each element is expected to be a list (sublist).\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary where keys are tuples (representing unique sublists)\n        and values are their corresponding counts.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input_list is not a list or if any element\n                   within input_list is not a list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of lists.\")\n\n    tuple_representations = []\n    for sublist in input_list:\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the input list must be lists (sublists).\")\n        tuple_representations.append(tuple(sublist))\n\n    occurrence_map = Counter(tuple_representations)\n    return dict(occurrence_map)"}
