{"task_id": "Mbpp/759", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef is_decimal(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if a string represents a decimal number with exactly two digits of precision.\n    It checks for an optional sign, one or more digits, a decimal point, and exactly two post-decimal digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BR1: Regex to match decimal numbers with exactly two digits of precision.\n    # Handles optional leading sign (+/-), at least one digit before '.', and exactly two digits after '.'.\n    pattern = r\"^[+-]?\\d+\\.\\d{2}$\"\n    return bool(re.fullmatch(pattern, input_string))\n```"}
