{"task_id": "Mbpp/762", "solution": "class BusinessRules:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates business logic for month validation and 30-day month identification.\"\"\"\n    MONTHS_WITH_30_DAYS = [4, 6, 9, 11]\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def isValidMonthNumber(month_number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a month number is within the valid range of 1 to 12.\"\"\"\n        return 1 <= month_number <= 12\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def isMonthIn30DayList(month_number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the month number is present in the list of 30-day months.\"\"\"\n        return month_number in BusinessRules.MONTHS_WITH_30_DAYS\n\ndef check_monthnumber_number(month_number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given month number corresponds to a month with 30 days.\n    Returns True for April (4), June (6), September (9), November (11); False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not BusinessRules.isValidMonthNumber(month_number):\n        return False\n    return BusinessRules.isMonthIn30DayList(month_number)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef find_min_diff(arr: Union[List[int], Tuple[int, ...]], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the given collection.\n    It sorts the array and then iterates through adjacent elements to find the minimum difference.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        current_diff = abs(sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i])\n        if current_diff == 0:\n            # A difference of 0 indicates duplicate elements, which is the smallest possible difference.\n            return 0\n        min_diff = min(min_diff, current_diff)\n\n    return int(min_diff)\n```"}
