{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    polite_count = 0\n    current_num = 1\n    while True:\n        # Check if current_num is a power of 2: x > 0 and (x & (x - 1)) == 0\n        is_power_of_two = current_num > 0 and (current_num & (current_num - 1)) == 0\n\n        if not is_power_of_two:\n            polite_count += 1\n            if polite_count == n:\n                return current_num\n        current_num += 1\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is equivalent to the nth non-power-of-2 number.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    num = 1\n    while count < n:\n        # Check if num is NOT a power of 2 using bitwise operation.\n        if (num & (num - 1)) != 0:\n            count += 1\n        if count == n:\n            return num\n        num += 1\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/766", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_wise(input_list: list) -> list[tuple[any, any]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list of all pairs of consecutive items in a given list.\n    Returns an empty list if input_list has fewer than two items.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_list) < 2:\n        return []\n\n    result_pairs = []\n    for i in range(len(input_list) - 1):\n        result_pairs.append((input_list[i], input_list[i+1]))\n    return result_pairs\n```"}
