{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "```python\ndef count_divisors(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the number of divisors of n is even.\n    Leverages the property that perfect squares have an odd number of divisors.\n    \"\"\"\n    sqrt_n = int(n**0.5)\n    is_perfect_square = (sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n)\n    # If n is a perfect square, its divisor count is odd, so return False.\n    # Otherwise, its divisor count is even, so return True.\n    return not is_perfect_square\n```"}
