{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef _sum_odd_up_to(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers up to n using a mathematical formula.\n    Returns 0 for n less than 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    k = (n + 1) // 2\n    return k * k\n\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Returns 0 if l > r or if no odd natural numbers are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    # Adjust l to ensure only natural numbers (positive integers) are considered.\n    l = max(1, l)\n\n    # If, after adjustment, the effective lower bound exceeds the upper bound, return 0.\n    if l > r:\n        return 0\n\n    sum_up_to_r = _sum_odd_up_to(r)\n    sum_up_to_l_minus_1 = _sum_odd_up_to(l - 1)\n\n    return sum_up_to_r - sum_up_to_l_minus_1\n```"}
