{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "The code for the `is_perfect_square` function is:\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_perfect_square(number: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is a perfect square.\n    A perfect square is a non-negative integer whose square root is also an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    # Based on the problem's implicit definition, perfect squares are integers.\n    if number != int(number):\n        return False\n    \n    n_int = int(number)\n    # Calculate the integer square root of the number.\n    root = math.isqrt(n_int)\n    \n    # Verify if the square of the calculated root equals the original integer.\n    return root * root == n_int\n```"}
