{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) based on its sum definition.\n    This function includes helper functions for combinations and factorial inline.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _combinations(n_val, k_val):\n        # Helper function to compute the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * _combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m + 1 - k)**n)\n        total_sum += term\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
