{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_common_divisors(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors of two given numbers.\n\n    This function finds the greatest common divisor (GCD) of num1 and num2,\n    then sums all positive divisors of that GCD.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate GCD using the Euclidean algorithm on absolute values.\n    a, b = abs(num1), abs(num2)\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    gcd_value = a\n\n    # Sum all positive divisors of the GCD.\n    sum_div = 0\n    for d in range(1, gcd_value + 1):\n        if gcd_value % d == 0:\n            sum_div += d\n    return sum_div\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring.\n    Applies Kadane's algorithm after transforming '0's to 1 and '1's to -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    transformed_array = []\n    for char in binary_string:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_array.append(1)\n        else:  # Assumes '1' due to critical requirement to trust caller's input.\n            transformed_array.append(-1)\n\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for num in transformed_array:\n        current_max += num\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n\n    return max_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "```python\ndef find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's\n    in any contiguous substring of the given binary string.\n    This uses an adaptation of Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_diff = 0\n    current_diff = 0\n\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            current_diff += 1\n        else:  # char is '1'\n            current_diff -= 1\n\n        # If current_diff becomes negative, reset it to 0 as\n        # a negative sum is detrimental to finding a maximum.\n        if current_diff < 0:\n            current_diff = 0\n\n        # Update the maximum difference found across all substrings.\n        max_diff = max(max_diff, current_diff)\n\n    return max_diff\n```"}
