{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef magic_square_test(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given 2D list (matrix) is a magic square.\n    A magic square has equal sums for all rows, columns, and both main diagonals.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_square_matrix(mat: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the input matrix is square and non-empty.\"\"\"\n        if not mat:\n            return False\n\n        n = len(mat)\n        for row in mat:\n            if len(row) != n:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _calculate_row_sums(mat: List[List[Union[int, float]]], size: int) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements for each row.\"\"\"\n        row_sums = [sum(row) for row in mat]\n        return row_sums\n\n    def _calculate_col_sums(mat: List[List[Union[int, float]]], size: int) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements for each column.\"\"\"\n        col_sums = [0] * size\n        for r_idx in range(size):\n            for c_idx in range(size):\n                col_sums[c_idx] += mat[r_idx][c_idx]\n        return col_sums\n\n    def _calculate_main_diagonal_sum(mat: List[List[Union[int, float]]], size: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the main diagonal (top-left to bottom-right).\"\"\"\n        main_diag_sum = 0\n        for i in range(size):\n            main_diag_sum += mat[i][i]\n        return main_diag_sum\n\n    def _calculate_anti_diagonal_sum(mat: List[List[Union[int, float]]], size: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the anti-diagonal (top-right to bottom-left).\"\"\"\n        anti_diag_sum = 0\n        for i in range(size):\n            anti_diag_sum += mat[i][size - 1 - i]\n        return anti_diag_sum\n\n    if not _is_square_matrix(matrix):\n        return False\n\n    n = len(matrix)\n\n    row_sums = _calculate_row_sums(matrix, n)\n    col_sums = _calculate_col_sums(matrix, n)\n    main_diag_sum = _calculate_main_diagonal_sum(matrix, n)\n    anti_diag_sum = _calculate_anti_diagonal_sum(matrix, n)\n\n    # Collect all sums into a single list\n    all_sums = row_sums + col_sums + [main_diag_sum, anti_diag_sum]\n\n    # Check if all collected sums are identical\n    if not all_sums: # This handles the N=0 case again, though _is_square_matrix already prevents it.\n        return False\n\n    # A set with one element implies all elements were equal.\n    return len(set(all_sums)) == 1\n\n```"}
