{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef max_occurrences(input_list: list) -> object:\n    \"\"\"Finds the item with the highest frequency in a list.\n    Returns any one of the most frequent items if there are ties.\"\"\"\n    counts = collections.Counter(input_list)\n\n    # If the list is empty, counts will be empty, and max(counts.values()) will raise ValueError.\n    # This behavior adheres to the constraint of not adding explicit error handling.\n    max_freq = max(counts.values())\n\n    for item, freq in counts.items():\n        if freq == max_freq:\n            return item\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/130", "solution": "def max_occurrences(input_list: list) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the item with the maximum frequency in the given list.\n    Counts item occurrences and returns the most frequent one.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for item in input_list:\n        counts[item] = counts.get(item, 0) + 1\n\n    most_frequent_item = None\n    max_count = -1\n\n    for item, count in counts.items():\n        if count > max_count:\n            max_count = count\n            most_frequent_item = item\n\n    return most_frequent_item"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "```python\ndef magic_square_test(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given square matrix of integers is a magic square.\"\"\"\n\n    # 2. Input Validation\n    n = len(matrix)\n    if n == 0:  # Return False for an empty matrix\n        return False\n\n    # Assumes matrix is not empty due to previous check.\n    m = len(matrix[0])\n    if m == 0:  # Return False for a matrix with empty rows\n        return False\n\n    if n != m:  # Return False if the matrix is not square\n        return False\n\n    # Check if all rows have uniform length\n    for row in matrix:\n        if len(row) != m:\n            return False\n\n    # 3. Calculate Magic Constant from the sum of the first row\n    magic_sum = sum(matrix[0])\n\n    # 4. Check Row Sums\n    for row in matrix:\n        if sum(row) != magic_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # 5. Check Column Sums\n    column_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            column_sums[j] += matrix[i][j]\n\n    for col_sum in column_sums:\n        if col_sum != magic_sum:\n            return False\n\n    # 6. Check Main Diagonal Sum (Top-Left to Bottom-Right)\n    main_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        main_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    if main_diag_sum != magic_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # 7. Check Anti-Diagonal Sum (Top-Right to Bottom-Left)\n    anti_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        anti_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n    if anti_diag_sum != magic_sum:\n        return False\n\n    # 8. If all checks pass, the matrix is a magic square\n    return True\n```\n"}
