{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "```python\ndef zero_count(numbers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to prevent division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    zeroes = 0\n    non_zeroes = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num == 0:\n            zeroes += 1\n        else:\n            non_zeroes += 1\n\n    if non_zeroes == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        return float(zeroes / non_zeroes)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "```python\ndef zero_count(array_of_integers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array of integers.\n    Handles edge cases for empty arrays or arrays with no non-zero elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    zero_count_result = 0\n    non_zero_count_result = 0\n\n    for element in array_of_integers:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_count_result += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count_result += 1\n\n    if zero_count_result == 0 and non_zero_count_result == 0:\n        return float('nan')\n    elif non_zero_count_result == 0:\n        return float('inf')\n    else:\n        return float(zero_count_result) / non_zero_count_result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    Returns True if positive and has more than one '1' bit in binary, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # A number is a power of 2 if (number > 0) and (number & (number - 1) == 0).\n    # This also means it has exactly one '1' bit in its binary representation.\n    if (number & (number - 1)) == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # If it's positive and not a power of 2, it must have more than one '1' bit.\n    return True\n```"}
