{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef _flip(arr: list[int], i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of elements from index 0 up to index `i` (inclusive) in the list `arr`.\"\"\"\n    arr[0 : i + 1] = arr[0 : i + 1][::-1]\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Searches for the index of the maximum element within the first `n` elements of the list `arr`.\"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        if arr[j] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[j]\n            max_idx = j\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts the input list `arr` in-place using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a reference to the now sorted list.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(arr, current_size)\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            _flip(arr, max_idx)\n            _flip(arr, current_size - 1)\n    return arr\n```"}
