{"task_id": "Mbpp/165", "solution": "```python\ndef count_char_position(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts characters where their 1-based alphabetical position matches their 1-based string position.\n    This function handles case-insensitivity and ignores non-alphabetic characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_english_alphabetic(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a given character is an English alphabet letter.\"\"\"\n        return 'a' <= char <= 'z'\n\n    def _get_alphabetical_position(char: str) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the 1-based alphabetical position of an English alphabet character.\"\"\"\n        return ord(char) - ord('a') + 1\n\n    match_count = 0\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        string_position = i + 1\n        char_lower = char.lower()\n\n        if _is_english_alphabetic(char_lower):\n            alphabetical_position = _get_alphabetical_position(char_lower)\n            if alphabetical_position == string_position:\n                match_count += 1\n    return match_count\n```"}
