{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers in a list whose bitwise XOR results in an even number.\n    Uses an O(N) single-pass approach to count even and odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(nums) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for number in nums:\n        if number % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # Calculate pairs from even numbers (Even ^ Even = Even)\n    even_pairs = even_count * (even_count - 1) // 2\n    # Calculate pairs from odd numbers (Odd ^ Odd = Even)\n    odd_pairs = odd_count * (odd_count - 1) // 2\n\n    return even_pairs + odd_pairs\n```"}
