{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef isMajority(arr: list[int], n: int, x: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element 'x' is a majority element in a sorted array 'arr' of length 'n'.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the first occurrence of x using binary search.\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_occurrence_index = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            first_occurrence_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Continue searching in the left half for the first occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # If x is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_occurrence_index == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Check if the element at first_occurrence_index + n // 2 is also x.\n    # If x is a majority element, this element must be x.\n    majority_check_index = first_occurrence_index + n // 2\n    if majority_check_index < n and arr[majority_check_index] == x:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n```"}
