{"task_id": "Mbpp/224", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Set_Bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts set bits in an integer. Handles negative numbers using a 32-bit two's complement interpretation.\n    This implementation uses Brian Kernighan's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    if number < 0:\n        # Mask to 32 bits for negative numbers to adhere to the design's 32-bit two's complement interpretation.\n        # For example, -1 becomes 0xFFFFFFFF (2^32 - 1).\n        number = number & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    while number > 0:\n        number &= (number - 1)\n        count += 1\n    return count\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef _find_first_occurrence(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of 'element' in 'array' using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the last occurrence of 'element' in 'array' using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the element is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(array: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, n, element)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, n, element)\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n    return count > n / 2\n```"}
