{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits of the input number to 1.\n    The mask extends to cover the number's bit length, ensuring a minimum of 16 bits.\"\"\"\n\n    # Calculate mask length: minimum 16 bits, or number's bit length if greater.\n    max_bits = max(16, number.bit_length() if number > 0 else 0)\n\n    even_mask = 0\n    # Create a mask with all even bits set up to max_bits.\n    for i in range(0, max_bits + 1, 2):\n        even_mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    return number | even_mask\n```"}
