{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def _calculate_increasing_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index.\n    dp_inc[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index i.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    dp_inc = list(arr)\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dp_inc[i] = max(dp_inc[i], dp_inc[j] + arr[i])\n    return dp_inc\n\ndef _calculate_decreasing_sums(arr: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each index.\n    dp_dec[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at index i.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    dp_dec = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dp_dec[i] = max(dp_dec[i], dp_dec[j] + arr[i])\n    return dp_dec\n\ndef max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Step 1: Calculate maximum increasing subsequence sum ending at each index\n    increasing_sums = _calculate_increasing_sums(arr)\n\n    # Step 2: Calculate maximum decreasing subsequence sum starting at each index\n    decreasing_sums = _calculate_decreasing_sums(arr)\n\n    # Step 3: Combine results to find the maximum bitonic subsequence sum\n    # A bitonic subsequence can be formed by combining an increasing subsequence\n    # ending at index i and a decreasing subsequence starting at index i.\n    # We subtract arr[i] once because it's included in both sums.\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum 