{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence (LPS) for the given string.\n    This function uses a dynamic programming approach.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of LPS of substring input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for current_len in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - current_len + 1):\n            j = i + current_len - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                if current_len == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence (LPS)\n    for the given input string using dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(input_string)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    for gap in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - gap + 1):\n            j = i + gap - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                if gap == 2:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
