{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "```python\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of valid integer sequences of length n.\n    Each element must be positive, greater than or equal to twice the previous, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, last_element: int, m: int, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively counts valid sequences starting from a given state.\n        Memoization is used to store and reuse results for subproblems.\n        \"\"\"\n        if (current_length, last_element) in memo:\n            return memo[(current_length, last_element)]\n\n        if current_length == n:\n            return 1  # A valid sequence of length n has been formed.\n\n        total_count_for_this_path = 0\n        start_next_element = 2 * last_element\n\n        for next_element in range(start_next_element, m + 1):\n            total_count_for_this_path += _count_sequences_recursive(current_length + 1, next_element, m, n)\n\n        memo[(current_length, last_element)] = total_count_for_this_path\n        return total_count_for_this_path\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1  # There is one empty sequence.\n    if n == 1:\n        return m  # Any integer from 1 to m can be the first element.\n\n    grand_total = 0\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        grand_total += _count_sequences_recursive(1, first_element, m, n)\n\n    return grand_total\n```"}
