{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "```python\ndef is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is a prime number.\n    Uses an optimized trial division method.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num <= 1:\n        return False\n    if num <= 3:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams number, validates input n,\n    checks if it is prime, and returns it or raises a ValueError.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input Validation as per design specification\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # NSW Number Calculation\n    if n == 0:\n        s_n = 1\n    elif n == 1:\n        s_n = 1\n    else:\n        s_k_minus_2 = 1  # Corresponds to S_0\n        s_k_minus_1 = 1  # Corresponds to S_1\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            s_n = 2 * s_k_minus_1 + s_k_minus_2\n            s_k_minus_2 = s_k_minus_1\n            s_k_minus_1 = s_n\n\n    # Primality Check and Return/Error Handling as per design specification\n    if is_prime(s_n):\n        return s_n\n    else:\n        raise ValueError(f\"S_{n} ({s_n}) is not prime.\")\n```"}
