{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "```python\ndef dog_age(human_years: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on human years.\n    Applies specific business rules for age conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if human_years <= 2:\n        # For the first two human years, the conversion rate is 10.5 dog years per human year.\n        # The result is cast to an integer.\n        return int(human_years * 10.5)\n    else:\n        # For human years greater than two, account for 21 dog years for the first two,\n        # plus 4 dog years for each subsequent human year.\n        return 21 + (human_years - 2) * 4\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef combinations_colors(elements_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[Tuple[Any, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all combinations with repetition of elements from the input list\n    with a specified length n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        return []\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    if not elements_list:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n\n    # Recursive helper function to build combinations.\n    # start_index ensures elements are picked in non-decreasing order of index, allowing repetition.\n    def _generate(current_combination: Tuple[Any, ...], start_index: int):\n        if len(current_combination) == n:\n            result.append(current_combination)\n            return\n\n        for i in range(start_index, len(elements_list)):\n            _generate(current_combination + (elements_list[i],), i)\n\n    _generate((), 0)\n    return result\n```"}
