{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(data_list: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of scores for each unique name. It then returns the name with the highest total score.\"\"\"\n    name_scores_map = {}\n\n    for name, score in data_list:\n        name_scores_map[name] = name_scores_map.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    if not name_scores_map:\n        return (None, 0)\n\n    # Find the name and score with the maximum aggregated score.\n    highest_name, highest_score = max(name_scores_map.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    return (highest_name, highest_score)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "```python\ndef _combinations(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\n    It computes 'n choose k', the number of ways to choose k items from n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    if k == 0 or k == n:\n        return 1\n    if k > n // 2:\n        k = n - k\n\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(k):\n        res = res * (n - i) // (i + 1)\n    return res\n\n\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of first n bits equals sum of last n bits.\n    This function sums (C(n, k))^2 for k from 0 to n.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        combinations_nk = _combinations(n, k)\n        total_count += combinations_nk * combinations_nk\n    return float(total_count)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(dictionary: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting level of dictionaries within the input dictionary. The depth is defined as the maximum level of nested dictionaries.\"\"\"\n\n    if not dictionary:\n        return 0\n\n    max_depth = 1\n\n    for value in dictionary.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            # Recursively calculate depth for nested dictionaries and update max_depth.\n            nested_depth = dict_depth(value)\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, nested_depth + 1)\n\n    return max_depth\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(input_dict: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting depth of dictionaries within the input dictionary.\n    The depth is 1 plus the maximum depth of any nested dictionary value.\"\"\"\n    max_current_depth = 1\n    for value in input_dict.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            # Recursively calculate depth for nested dictionaries\n            nested_depth = dict_depth(value)\n            max_current_depth = max(max_current_depth, 1 + nested_depth)\n    return max_current_depth\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\ndef start_withp(input_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first two words starting with 'p' (case-insensitive) from a list of strings.\n    Pads the result with empty strings if fewer than two qualifying words are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    collected_words = []\n\n    for input_string in input_list:\n        # StringProcessor logic: split the input string into individual words\n        words = input_string.split()\n\n        for word in words:\n            # WordFilter logic: check if the word starts with 'p' case-insensitively\n            if word.lower().startswith('p'):\n                collected_words.append(word)\n                # Stop processing once two words are found\n                if len(collected_words) == 2:\n                    break\n        # If two words are found, exit the outer loop as well\n        if len(collected_words) == 2:\n            break\n\n    # Pad with empty strings if fewer than two words were collected\n    while len(collected_words) < 2:\n        collected_words.append('')\n\n    return tuple(collected_words)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\ndef _extract_all_words(string_list: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits each string in the input list into individual words and returns a flat list of all words.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_words = []\n    for s in string_list:\n        all_words.extend(s.split())\n    return all_words\n\ndef _is_p_word(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given word starts with 'p' or 'P' (case-insensitive).\n    \"\"\"\n    return len(word) > 0 and word[0].lower() == 'p'\n\ndef start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts words from a list of strings and returns the first two words that start with 'p' (case-insensitive) as a tuple.\n    If fewer than two words are found, the tuple is padded with None.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_words = _extract_all_words(word_list)\n    p_words_found = []\n\n    for word in all_words:\n        if _is_p_word(word):\n            p_words_found.append(word)\n            if len(p_words_found) == 2:\n                break\n\n    first_p_word = p_words_found[0] if len(p_words_found) > 0 else None\n    second_p_word = p_words_found[1] if len(p_words_found) > 1 else None\n\n    return (first_p_word, second_p_word)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[float], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i] plus arr[k],\n    where the last element of the prefix subsequence is less than arr[k].\n    \"\"\"\n    max_prefix_sum = 0.0\n    arr_k_value = arr[k]\n\n    dp = [0.0] * (i + 1)\n\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[idx] = arr[idx]\n        for prev_idx in range(idx):\n            if arr[idx] > arr[prev_idx]:\n                dp[idx] = max(dp[idx], dp[prev_idx] + arr[idx])\n\n        # Condition Check: last element of subsequence (arr[idx]) must be less than arr[k]\n        if arr[idx] < arr_k_value:\n            max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, dp[idx])\n\n    if max_prefix_sum > 0.0:\n        final_sum = max_prefix_sum + arr_k_value\n    else:\n        # If no valid prefix subsequence is found, the sum is just arr[k]\n        final_sum = arr_k_value\n\n    return final_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from a prefix 0..i including arr[k].\"\"\"\n\n    # Input Validation\n    if n != len(arr):\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be equal to the length of arr.\")\n    if not (0 <= i < n):\n        raise ValueError(\"i must be within the bounds of the array (0 to n-1).\")\n    if not (0 <= k < n):\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be within the bounds of the array (0 to n-1).\")\n    if not (k > i):\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be strictly greater than i.\")\n\n    kth_element_value = arr[k]\n    prefix_elements_for_subsequence = []\n\n    # Filter Prefix Elements from arr[0] to arr[i] (inclusive)\n    # Only elements smaller than kth_element_value can be part of the increasing subsequence before kth_element_value.\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[idx] < kth_element_value:\n            prefix_elements_for_subsequence.append(arr[idx])\n\n    # Calculate max sum from the filtered prefix elements\n    max_prefix_sum = 0\n    if prefix_elements_for_subsequence:\n        dp_prefix = list(prefix_elements_for_subsequence)\n\n        for x in range(len(prefix_elements_for_subsequence)):\n            for y in range(x):\n                if prefix_elements_for_subsequence[x] > prefix_elements_for_subsequence[y]:\n                    dp_prefix[x] = max(dp_prefix[x], dp_prefix[y] + prefix_elements_for_subsequence[x])\n\n        max_prefix_sum = max(dp_prefix)\n\n    # Aggregate Result: add the mandatory kth element's value\n    return max_prefix_sum + kth_element_value\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\ndef large_product(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n largest products formed by pairing elements from two lists.\n    It computes all possible products, sorts them, and returns the top n.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n\n    # Generate all possible products\n    for x in list1:\n        for y in list2:\n            all_products.append(x * y)\n\n    # Sort products in descending order\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the first n largest products\n    return all_products[:n]\n```"}
