{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "class MinHeap:\n    \"\"\"\n    A min-heap implementation used to efficiently store and retrieve the smallest element.\n    It supports push, pop, peek, and size operations.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._heap = []\n\n    def _sift_up(self, idx):\n        \"\"\"Moves an element up the heap to maintain the min-heap property.\"\"\"\n        parent_idx = (idx - 1) // 2\n        while idx > 0 and self._heap[idx] < self._heap[parent_idx]:\n            self._heap[idx], self._heap[parent_idx] = self._heap[parent_idx], self._heap[idx]\n            idx = parent_idx\n            parent_idx = (idx - 1) // 2\n\n    def _sift_down(self, idx):\n        \"\"\"Moves an element down the heap to maintain the min-heap property.\"\"\"\n        n = len(self._heap)\n        left_child_idx = 2 * idx + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * idx + 2\n        smallest_idx = idx\n\n        if left_child_idx < n and self._heap[left_child_idx] < self._heap[smallest_idx]:\n            smallest_idx = left_child_idx\n        if right_child_idx < n and self._heap[right_child_idx] < self._heap[smallest_idx]:\n            smallest_idx = right_child_idx\n\n        if smallest_idx != idx:\n            self._heap[idx], self._heap[smallest_idx] = self._heap[smallest_idx], self._heap[idx]\n            self._sift_down(smallest_idx)\n\n    def push(self, item):\n        \"\"\"Adds an item to the heap and maintains the min-heap property.\"\"\"\n        self._heap.append(item)\n        self._sift_up(len(self._heap) - 1)\n\n    def pop(self):\n        \"\"\"Removes and returns the smallest item from the heap.\"\"\"\n        if not self._heap:\n            return None # Should not happen based on design usage\n\n        if len(self._heap) == 1:\n            return self._heap.pop()\n\n        smallest = self._heap[0]\n        self._heap[0] = self._heap.pop()\n        self._sift_down(0)\n        return smallest\n\n    def peek(self):\n        \"\"\"Returns the smallest item in the heap without removing it.\"\"\"\n        if not self._heap:\n            return None\n        return self._heap[0]\n\n    def size(self):\n        \"\"\"Returns the number of elements in the heap.\"\"\"\n        return len(self._heap)\n\n\ndef large_product(list1, list2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k largest products formed by pairing elements from two lists.\n    Products are returned in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_heap = MinHeap()\n\n    for x in list1:\n        for y in list2:\n            product = x * y\n            if min_heap.size() < k:\n                min_heap.push(product)\n            elif product > min_heap.peek():\n                min_heap.pop()\n                min_heap.push(product)\n\n    # Extract all elements from the heap\n    result = []\n    while min_heap.size() > 0:\n        result.append(min_heap.pop())\n\n    # Sort in descending order as requested\n    result.sort(reverse=True)\n    return result"}
