{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    Uses an iterative approach based on L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2).\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            next_lucas = a + b\n            a = b\n            b = next_lucas\n        return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit of the input integer.\n    Example: set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    temp_num = number\n    bit_pos = 0\n    # Find the position one greater than the most significant set bit.\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        temp_num >>= 1\n        bit_pos += 1\n\n    # Iterate from this highest bit position downwards to find the leftmost unset bit.\n    for i in range(bit_pos - 1, -1, -1):\n        mask = 1 << i\n        if (number & mask) == 0:\n            return number | mask\n\n    # If all bits up to the MSB are set, the leftmost unset bit is at the next position.\n    return number | (1 << bit_pos)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "```python\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    For non-positive n, it returns 1 (representing 2^0).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 1\n\n    power = 1\n    # Iteratively double the power until the next power exceeds n.\n    while (power << 1) <= n:\n        power <<= 1\n    return power\n```"}
