{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo: dict[int, int] = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum f(n) using memoization.\n    f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n) using integer division.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate the sum of subproblems\n    sum_of_sub_problems = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_sub_problems, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n# Module-level cache for memoization, storing previously computed results.\n_memo = {}\n\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum for a non-negative integer n using a specified recursive formula.\n    It employs memoization to avoid redundant computations, with f(0) = 0 as the base case.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    else:\n        # Recursively calculate sums of subproblems using integer division.\n        sum_sub_results = (get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n                           get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n                           get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n                           get_max_sum(n // 5))\n        result = max(sum_sub_results, n)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
