{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\nclass sum_digits_calculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    A utility class to compute sums of digits for numbers.\n    It includes a method for a single number and another for a list of numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_single_number_sum_of_digits(self, number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the sum of digits for a single integer.\n        Uses modulo and integer division to extract and sum digits.\n        \"\"\"\n        current_number = number\n        digit_sum = 0\n        while current_number > 0:\n            digit_sum += current_number % 10\n            current_number //= 10\n        return digit_sum\n\n    def sum_of_digits(self, numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the total sum of digits for a list of numbers.\n        It iterates through the list, summing digits for each number.\n        \"\"\"\n        total_sum_of_individual_sums = 0\n        for number in numbers:\n            total_sum_of_individual_sums += self._calculate_single_number_sum_of_digits(number)\n        return total_sum_of_individual_sums\n\n```"}
