{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "def min_product_tuple(data_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum product from pairs of integers within a given list of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        data_list: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains exactly two integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        The minimum product found among all tuples in the `data_list`.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the `data_list` is empty or if any tuple within `data_list`\n                    does not contain exactly two integers, or if elements within a tuple\n                    are not integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data_list:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(data_list):\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple) or len(item) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Element at index {i} must be a tuple of two integers.\")\n        if not isinstance(item[0], int) or not isinstance(item[1], int):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Elements within the tuple at index {i} must be integers.\")\n\n    min_product = data_list[0][0] * data_list[0][1]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(data_list)):\n        a, b = data_list[i]\n        current_product = a * b\n        if current_product < min_product:\n            min_product = current_product\n\n    return min_product"}
